        "original_id": "17afeee7-1422-54d2-8cea-2374b31fe8f6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Morgan Paull, Ridley Scott, Hampton Fancher, David Peoples, Philip K. Dick\n- Products: Blade Runner, Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?, Dirty O'Neil\n- Roles: Dave Holden, Jimmy O'Neil\n- Places: Texas\n\nFacts:\n- Philip K. Dick wrote the 1968 novel \"Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?\"\n- \"Blade Runner\" was written by Hampton Fancher and David Peoples, and it is a loose adaptation of Philip K. Dick's 1968 novel \"Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?\"\n- Morgan Paull was born on December 15, 1944, and he was an American actor.\n- In Ridley Scott's film \"Blade Runner,\" Morgan Paull is most notable for playing Dave Holden.\n- In \"Dirty O'Neil,\" Morgan Paull plays Jimmy O'Neil, a cop in a small Texas town who is forced into action when three homicidal thugs invade the town.\n- Morgan Paull died on July 17, 2012.",
